{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested: PD-1 archive restart procedure, head 8ad7c7b14b4ca84d1f4070ef0a6727306e7a4b15, tree f3993750 (branch planner/archive-restart-runbook-20261025, one commit on Main f5a6338c; delta examples/grow/runbook.md only, +235). Review request fde66ef5, checker promise 33921484, request 2f653384.\n\nI checked the section against the source on Main 2f5d9a2f. Main moved there at 12:19 (Room A fixed-next-prefix landing). The section lands on that Main, and archive-driver.ts and archive-row.ts changed in it.\n\nVerified, no change needed:\n- Worked example. Using the repository's own canonicalize and digestBytes, I composed the row as steps 2 and 3 say (v, at, repository, format, confirmed with anchorsPublished and layout 2, pending null, attempts 0, next null, stopped limit/null). Its digest is sha256:8a148e2b…, equal to rowDigest. The directive without command digests to sha256:1a96ec60…, equal to command. The canonical value is 757 bytes. The real readArchiveRestart accepts it before 06:30:00Z and refuses it at 06:30:00Z, and refuses the same directive with a .000 fraction. The two unseen-field variants (anchorsPublished absent, where \"plan\") do not match, as step 3 implies.\n- Row fields match ArchiveRow; directive fields, 8,192-byte limit, canonical form and expiry check match archive-restart.ts. Restart admission in ArchiveRows.restart matches steps 1 to 4: reason limit, no pending Mark, attempts 0, next null, layout 2, repository, format and confirmed equal, rowDigest over the stored bytes, generation equal to the receipt. An applied restart clears the stop, writes the wake with next one second ahead (#later(0)) and raises the generation by one; a later activation with the same command at generation + 1 returns already-applied. rowDigest appears only for a limit stop with no pending Mark (archive-operator.ts).\n- Activation order (diagnostic, then the directive, then alarm recovery; refused while an alarm or driver is running) matches object.ts and ArchiveDriver.restart. Only worker.grow.ts passes ARCHIVE_RESTART_DIRECTIVE.\n- Backoff: min(300, 1 × 2^count) seconds with production bounds 1 and 300; the count saturates at 32 and a confirmation resets it.\n- dap scope-index inventory --out FILE and sweep --manifest FILE match scope-index-command.ts; the inventory records each scope's at. repository id and name equal repositoryName in GROW_ARCHIVE_CONFIG.\n- Product names: the runbook already names Cloudflare, Wrangler and MCP for operations; the section is consistent with it. No comparisons.\n\nGaps to fix:\n1. Field table, reason. The diagnostic reports any of the 25 reasons in archive-operator.ts (for example limit, timeout, unavailable, mismatch, parent, foreign-source-unavailable, rebuild-mismatch), and unknown for anything else. The row says \"limit, timeout or unavailable\". Say that only limit can be restarted.\n2. Field table, storedWake. archiveRowDiagnostic projects the wake to pending, stopped and next only, so capacityDeferrals never appears in the line. Remove \"A deferred row also carries capacityDeferrals\". In \"Tell a deferral from a stop\", say how a deferral shows: the pass line has state retry, reason limit and a capacityRefusal, and the row line shows storedWake pending true, stopped false and a next time.\n3. \"Tell a deferral from a stop\" is out of date for Main 2f5d9a2f. After a capacity deferral, the next pass of a published row archives exactly the next entry. Its pass line carries fixedFinish (used, remaining, metadataMargin 65,536). A refused fixed pass shows capacityRefusal site finish-affordability, kind finish-quote, reserved metadata 65,536. Also, a limit stop can still happen after the deferral landed: a null finish quote, or a debit outside lookahead (capacityRefusal site plan-debit), stops the row with reason limit. Those rows are the ones a directive is for. The sentence \"A row that stopped before the deferral landed, or that stopped for a reason other than capacity\" says otherwise. Base the head on 2f5d9a2f (or merge it) and add fixedFinish to the pass-line fields.\n4. Refusal causes. Add: the scope is not active (object.ts applies the directive only when the scope's status is active). Optionally add the policy registry being empty, which also refuses.\n5. Removal step. \"Every plain setting of dap-grow is in wrangler.grow.jsonc\" cannot be confirmed from the repository. docs/deploy.md says --keep-vars keeps settings the file omits and that reviewed --var overrides may exist. The Worker code reads ARTIFACTS_NAMESPACE and DEMO_START_CONFIG, which wrangler.grow.jsonc does not set. Replace the sentence with a required check: read the live version's settings, list every plain setting that is not in the file, and either carry each one on the removal command as a reviewed --var or stop. Keep the versions view check afterwards.\n\nNonblocking:\n- Say where the repository host comes from: the Destination's repository item. Do not imply it is ARTIFACTS_CONFIG's host, which is a different value.\n- The tail wrapper is described but not named; name the one the planner uses, or give the timeout command.\n- Rewrap the first paragraph; two lines run well past the file's width.\n\nArchitecture: the procedure follows the restart design: one row per directive, bound to row bytes, generation and expiry, applied once. Security: correct. The section says that only the deploying principal can restart, and that no member, route or MCP tool can. It publishes no secret, and the example contains only public identifiers. Simplification: well ordered. Gaps 1 to 3 are errors of fact for the operator, not style.\n\nGate: the planner's run at 8ad7c7b1 (3,585 passed, 3 skipped) is cited; I did not inspect its log. A new head needs its own gate as docs/testing.md requires.\n\nVerdict: changes requested at 8ad7c7b1 / f3993750 for gaps 1 to 5.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:eed5c8394fc4ba9d5d50b620333630d01608beaf","binding":"assigned","head":"8ad7c7b14b4ca84d1f4070ef0a6727306e7a4b15","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:33921484956bcae11f56d24ab57bcbc85dc0708e\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:ebf9f91c1568babb1aa76418313573be323ce9f6\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:42506bdb641d9872b5d9d09a77eb66b00890e8c0","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}